{"authored" [{"question" "q-34602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$, if $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-34602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 8[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-8[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-2k=24\\,⟹\\,k=-12.\n$$\n\nBut then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $k$ such that \n $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/ques