answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third  equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} & =-16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+{x}_{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ (-2)+2(3) & =3 \\\\ 4 & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73951" 