"value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3}=-18 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -15 & -30\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{15}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this value into  the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2(2)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(2) & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=1$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=2,$ which means \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-2)+2=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "3693b0643c1637beb0ed893dfd77bc3fee5e50bf0bbf7e312c52cf34eea746d7" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $s,$ if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/df62636427555a986454d8d2787e110eb664771f5a74a38fdaa99ec593643729.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4789.json" "file_sha256" "2f2b238e048cec206630c25379400cd06343af81483b5983561a7d7c4beb883c" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+s{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4789.json" "file_sha256" "2f2b238e048cec206630c25379400cd06343af81483b5983561a7d7c4beb883c" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\mathbf{x},$ if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/0e6491c477a442fc9dae1462413d593815a6761393ad3a0d2f8d72de665a7c93.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4790.json" "file_sha256" "5390b86fa6c93a11f2212613512364496bbcd3e59bca58363af1429af397957e" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4790.json" "file_sha256" "5390b86fa6c93a11f2212613512364496bbcd3e59bca58363af1429af397957e" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/e9e0ea8fb6e9ba5f4595f15efe4f04e93db373dbc020f5672db34d5a3c12024b.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then what is $x_1+x_2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4791.json" "file_sha256" "af5ffa41d7cdec673526d87c837b7923dffc92c9ac5b6d0070c82145d07aed14" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain $x_1=5,$ which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 4(5)+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3(5)+(-15) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15,$ which means\n\n$$\n5 \\mathbf{c_1}-15 \\mathbf{c_2} = \\mathbf{d}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2=5-15=-10.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4791.json" "file_sha256" "af5ffa41d7cdec673526d87c837b7923dffc92c9ac5b6d0070c82145d07aed14" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/4749f1e50cf7768f39d26737bfce4d9e8e85d5b350f4bc9844a358cd4c3c5cc0.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf b,$ then what is $x_1+x_2+x_3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-6191.json" "file_sha256" "69790720315e2794dcc498c28fc23d3b0345d43ca733102d0c16b1a4c4f323bd" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/a4e5c5eba6d2d8b30955668d47bb2a131c702cc7ec62ef7dada9ed9ad60d8182.png)\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-6191.json" "file_sha256" "69790720315e2794dcc498c28fc23d3b0345d43ca733102d0c16b1a4c4f323bd" "basis" 1628 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-34051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$, if $2{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-34051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+k[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $k=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-34051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a70cb16ea7c938975cb7f05d7d1eb3f8f5c1010f3b7770c1c30064bcb693fa5f"} {"question" "q-34051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question"