attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a-5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -22 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-34052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-5x & =b \\\\ -5x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}([\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -22 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3-1=-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-34052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a70cb16ea7c938975cb7f05d7d1eb3f8f5c1010f3b7770c1c30064bcb693fa5f"} {"question" "q-34052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"}