ategory" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a70cb16ea7c938975cb7f05d7d1eb3f8f5c1010f3b7770c1c30064bcb693fa5f"} {"question" "q-73936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-73936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-73936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-105161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$ given that $7a+4x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-105161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7a+4x & =b \\\\ 4x & =b-7a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}(b-7a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-2-1=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-105161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a70cb16ea7c938975cb7f05d7d1eb3f8f5c1010f3b7770c1c30064bcb693fa5f"} {"question" "q-105161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-105161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-105161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third  equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} & =-16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+{x}_{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ (-2)+2(3) & =3 \\\\ 4 & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a70cb16ea7c938975cb7f05d7d1eb3f8f5c1010f3b7770c1c30064bcb693fa5f"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-34568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "q-34568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13{x}_{2} & =13\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4(1) & =3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=1$ into the third equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 5(1)+2(1) & =5 \\\\ 7 & =5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082816/state.json" "file_sha256" "d981bc78b4b52e0e3b5a626533c540cb0f8af4ae2955e0066dce541080e46812"} {"question" "